meta {
  name: Get Admission Cycle Status (Student)
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/{{admissionCycleId}}/application/status
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Full cycle-level admission status — application progress, assessment,
  interview, and token/offer amount details — one entry per Application
  the student has here (there can be several now, one per course, see
  Start Application).

  `data` is `null` if the student hasn't started any application for this
  admission cycle yet. Otherwise an array, each entry shaped:

  {
    application: {
      applicationId, applicationNumber,
      collegeId, collegeName,
      admissionCycleId, admissionCycleName,
      formStatus, feePaymentStatus,
      pendingAction: "payment" | "personal_details" | "family_details"
                   | "address_details" | "qualification_details"
                   | "declaration" | "submit" | "none",
      // Every non-withdrawn course on this application, not just the
      // primary. isShortlisted is the only per-course field here (a
      // student can be shortlisted for one course on an application but
      // not another) — everything else below is whole-application.
      courses: [
        { courseId, courseName, courseCode, isPrimary, status, isShortlisted }, ...
      ],
      createdAt
    },

    // One assessment attempt covers the WHOLE application (every course
    // on it), not one per course — see Plan R.
    assessment: {
      status: "not_required" | "not_started" | "in_progress" | "completed"
            | "auto_submitted" | "terminated" | "under_evaluation"
            | "evaluated" | "result_published",
      attemptId, startedAt, completedAt, totalScore, maxScore
    },

    // Whole-application, not per-course — a student interviews once for
    // the application, resolved off its primary course's booking.
    interview: {
      status: "not_scheduled" | "booked" | "completed" | "cancelled" | "rescheduled",
      scheduledAt, completedAt, outcome, score, remarks
    },

    // Whole-application, resolved off the primary course's offer letter.
    amountDetails: {
      status: "not_issued" | "issued" | "expired" | "withdrawn",
      offerNumber, tokenAmount, tokenPaymentStatus, validUntil, documentUrl
    }
  }

  pendingAction — the single next thing to do for this application, not a
  list of everything remaining:
  - primary course's fee not yet paid -> "payment"
  - paid, still draft -> the first incomplete step's name (e.g.
    "qualification_details"), derived cheaply from the application's
    currentStep (never re-checks whether an earlier step was actually
    filled in)
  - paid, currentStep past declaration -> "submit" (ready to call Submit
    Application)
  - formStatus "submitted" -> "none"

  Documents are NOT part of this sequence (Submit doesn't require them and
  currentStep doesn't track them) — check List Required/Uploaded Documents
  separately for that.

  interview and amountDetails will show "not_scheduled"/"not_issued" (all
  detail fields null) for every application today — the interviews and
  offer-letter backend modules aren't built yet (schema-only). This
  response shape is final; those sections will start returning real data
  automatically once those modules exist, with no further contract change.
}
